---
name: perf-measurement-setup
description: "How app speed was measured for PR #133 and the non-obvious findings (React cache in route handlers, nav boundaries)"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: c8e54f01-e87f-48cc-9ab8-c9b953ce4fcd
  modified: 2026-10-31T21:31:37.757Z
---

Speed work (PR #133, 2026-10-31) was measured on a production build (`next build && next start`), not `next dev`; dev compile time makes every page look slow.

- QA workspace is empty after `--reset`; seed it by importing a Revolut-format CSV (recognized without AI, so no model call needed).
- React `cache()` does not memoize in route handlers (chat, artifact frame): use `lib/per-client.ts` for per-request sharing there.
- `requireWorkspace()` runs again on every call inside route handlers; chat route tests deliberately pin the extra scope re-checks, so don't remove them.
- `staleTimes.dynamic` was tried and reverted: back navigation to pages older than the stale time re-renders them (Home back 34 ms to 886 ms); with 0, back is always instant.
- Pre-launch: the user allows breaking old artifacts/data for speed (2026-11-01).

**How to apply:** benchmark on a prod build with seeded data before claiming a speedup; measure against the moneo-qa stack (`npm run qa:server -- --production`, port 3100), see [[qa-backend-and-nightly-decisions]].
import { execFileSync, spawn } from "node:child_process";
import { existsSync, readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { parseEnv } from "node:util";

if (!existsSync(".env.qa")) throw new Error("No .env.qa: run `npm run setup -- --qa` first.");
const qa = parseEnv(readFileSync(".env.qa", "utf8"));
const names = file => existsSync(file) ? [...readFileSync(file, "utf8").matchAll(/^#?\s*([A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*)=/gm)].map(match => match[1]) : [];
const blank = Object.fromEntries([...names(".env.example"), ...names(".env")].map(name => [name, ""]));
const port = process.env.QA_PORT ?? "3100";
if (!/^\d+$/.test(port) || port === "3000") throw new Error("QA_PORT must be a free port other than 3000, which is the owner's app (AGENTS.md Test backend).");
const paid = process.env.E2E_REAL_AI === "1" ? {} : { OPENAI_API_KEY: "sk-qa-placeholder-not-a-real-key", OPENROUTER_API_KEY: "" };
const env = {
  ...process.env, ...blank, ...qa, ...paid,
  ENABLE_BANKING_APP_ID: "", ENABLE_BANKING_PRIVATE_KEY: "",
  PORT: port, NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL: `http://localhost:${port}`, WORKFLOW_LOCAL_BASE_URL: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`, NEXT_DIST_DIR: ".next-qa",
};
const next = "node_modules/next/dist/bin/next";
const production = process.argv.includes("--production");
if (production) execFileSync(process.execPath, [next, "build"], { env, stdio: "inherit" });
const server = spawn(process.execPath, [next, production ? "start" : "dev", "-H", "127.0.0.1", "-p", port], { env, stdio: "inherit" });
for (const signal of ["SIGINT", "SIGTERM"]) process.on(signal, () => server.kill(signal));
server.on("exit", code => process.exit(code ?? 0));

